    "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
    "extraction_notes": "Text-layer table. Column grid and row bands recovered from the raster rule lines (pdftoppm -r 200); marks binned mechanically from pdftotext -bbox token centres and diffed against a visual read of the rendered page; no disagreement. TWO leading label columns ('Time' and 'Assessment'), so the first data column is position 3 and the 20 data columns run 3-22. The 'Time' column holds one vertically merged cell reading 'Pre HD' covering all 13 assessment rows; it is a row-label column, not a schedule column, so it is carried as annotation t1 with one marker_location per covered row. Footnotes a-g are printed on document page 35, which carries no activity rows."
  },
  "table_metadata": {
    "table_number": 2,
    "table_type": "domain",
    "table_title": "Table 1b. Schedule of Laboratory Assessments",
    "table_purpose": "Laboratory assessments on the same study-visit timeline as Table 1a.",
    "page_start": 34,
    "page_end": 35,
    "notes": "Classified domain, not track or subsidiary: the 20 data columns are byte-identical to Table 1a's (Screening, -2, 1 ... 55, with the same (HD) qualifiers and the same combined 29/ET column), the participants are the same subjects, and the rows are a different assessment category (laboratory). It is not a continuation - Table 1a ends with its own bottom rule and its own footnote block, and this table restates the whole header. The extra 'Time' label column does not change the timeline granularity, so subsidiary does not apply. Document page 35 carries only the footnote block and contributes no activity rows."
  },
